{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "kZvcWrvG8F", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-09", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 907668, "segment_id": "Sz6VrO1yNV", "segment_broadcast_id": "kZvcWrvG8F", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction Charles Gibson (Racine, Wisconsin)", "segment_description": null, "segment_duration": 50, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 907668, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "kZvcWrvG8F", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-09", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 907668, "segment_id": "YhfspF7VP7", "segment_broadcast_id": "kZvcWrvG8F", "segment_title": "Economy: Stock Market / Sonders Interview", "segment_description": "(Racine, Wisconsin: Charles Gibson)  Today's huge drop in the stock market with a 40 percent drop in one calendar year reported  \n\n(Studio: Dan Harris)  The drop in the market despite the passage of the bailout plan and a global interest cut featured; scenes shown from the floor of the New York Stock Exchange; details given about the price of General Motors and energy and financial stocks.  [Jefferies and Co. strategist Art HOGAN&#134;- says it's a panic and crash; links the drop to mutual funds.]  The Treasury Department's consideration of direct cash deposits in banks to enable the banks to make loans to get the economy to move noted; diagram shown.  [President BUSH&nbsp- comments on taking strong action.]  [Trader Alan VALDES&#134;- reacts to the rate cuts and bailout.]  \n\n(Racine, Wisconsin: Charles Gibson)  Earlier discussion held with Charles Schwab investment strategist Liz Ann Sonders&#134; about the market.  [SONDERS&nbsp- assesses the market environment in the last couple of weeks making a lot of people flee the market; comments on the traders being scared, too.] ", "segment_duration": 310, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63050.0", "legacy_segment_id": 907669, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "kZvcWrvG8F", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-09", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 907668, "segment_id": "vZPmGW1xdg", "segment_broadcast_id": "kZvcWrvG8F", "segment_title": "Campaign 2008 / Obama vs. McCain / McCain Interview", "segment_description": "(Racine and Milwaukee, Wisconsin: Charles Gibson)  Today's exclusive ABC interview with Senator John McCain presented.  [On the ABC bus, McCAIN&nbsp- says we are in a crisis of unprecedented proportions so the Treasury should buy up bad mortgages to let people have affordable payment levels; outlines the financing for his plan to stop the fall of housing values; compares today's situation to the Great Depression; states they want mature and experienced leadership like that from President Franklin Roosevelt; reiterates Americans' faith and confidence is shaken; notes this is a tough campaign and he is the underdog playing the hand he was dealt; reasserts not enough is known about Senator Barack Obama, who launched his political career in the living room of William Ayers.]   (Racine, Wisconsin: Charles Gibson)  The McCain-Governor Sarah Palin rally in Milwaukee earlier in the day 